---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="For school and college ceramics departments"
	description="Wheel booking between classes, kiln firing queues and semester courses for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Schools &amp; colleges</p>
				<h1>One kiln or two. A whole semester of students.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Students book a wheel between lessons, every piece has its place in the firing queue, and
					your classes run from the timetable you already have.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheels booked between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks from their
			phone, so a free period turns into throwing time instead of a queue at the door. You decide how
			many hours each group gets a week and how far ahead they can book.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">More on wheel time</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Firings that keep up with the semester</h2>
		<p>
			With one or two kilns, everything goes through the same queue. Students log a piece when they
			set it on the bisque shelf, you see how full each load is, and they get a text when their work
			is ready to collect. The firing log keeps the date, cone and schedule for every load.
			<a href="/features/firings">More on kiln firings</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes that follow your timetable</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course once as a fixed series for the semester, add drop-in sessions for open
			studio, and let waitlists fill any seat that frees up. Instructors get their own roster and can
			mark attendance from the studio tablet.
			<a href="/features/classes">More on classes</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan?</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns, which fits most school and college departments with room
			to grow. If you only have one kiln, Starter covers it.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
			<div class="faq">
				<details>
					<summary>Is the Studio plan enough for our department?</summary>
					<p>
						The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns with unlimited members, so a department with one or
						two kilns fits comfortably. If you add a fourth kiln, you can move to Collective at any
						point in the month and we prorate the difference.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Do schools get a discount?</summary>
					<p>
						Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
						when you book a demo.
					</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can we import our class lists?</summary>
					<p>
						Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
					</p>
				</details>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your studio ready for next semester.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
